WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:32.125
<b>Here, Krishna explains that </b>

2
00:00:32.125 --> 00:00:41.250
<b>mere control over senses isn't enough </b>
<b>if attachments aren't fundamentally destroyed. </b>

3
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:47.458
<b>The senses are so restless that they </b>
<b>can distract even a wise person's mind,</b>

4
00:00:47.458 --> 00:00:51.750
<b>breaking their concentration.</b>

5
00:00:56.583 --> 00:00:59.291
<b>In the previous verse, Krishna explained</b>

6
00:00:59.291 --> 00:01:01.291
<b>that while an ordinary person</b>

7
00:01:01.291 --> 00:01:08.916
<b>can temporarily control their senses </b>
<b>by keeping away from sensory objects, </b>

8
00:01:08.916 --> 00:01:14.333
<b>this doesn't fully eliminate attachments.</b>

9
00:01:14.333 --> 00:01:17.833
<b>Past experiences remain etched in memory.</b>

10
00:01:17.833 --> 00:01:23.791
<b>And these senses can not only make </b>
<b>the mind yearn for old experiences</b>

11
00:01:23.791 --> 00:01:27.708
<b>but also make it fearful of them.</b>

12
00:01:27.708 --> 00:01:30.000
<b>Think of it this way</b>

13
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.708
<b>something unpleasant </b>
<b>happened to you in the past.</b>

14
00:01:32.708 --> 00:01:39.250
<b>the mind has preserved that experience.</b>

15
00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:42.250
<b>When a similar situation arises in the future,</b>

16
00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:46.416
<b>the mind immediately signals potential danger.</b>

17
00:01:46.416 --> 00:01:48.333
<b>There's a common saying</b>

18
00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:52.416
<b>"One who's been burnt by milk, </b>
<b>blows on buttermilk before drinking."</b>

19
00:01:52.416 --> 00:01:54.791
<b>This perfectly illustrates</b>

20
00:01:54.791 --> 00:01:58.208
<b>how someone whose tongue </b>
<b>was burnt by hot milk</b>

21
00:01:58.208 --> 00:02:00.416
<b>becomes cautious even with cold buttermilk</b>

22
00:02:00.416 --> 00:02:08.125
<b>the mind fears another burn </b>
<b>at the mere sight of a white liquid.</b>

23
00:02:08.125 --> 00:02:09.750
<b>The mind is incredibly fickle </b>

24
00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:12.166
<b>it brings up old fears,</b>

25
00:02:12.166 --> 00:02:15.375
<b>creating obstacles in new endeavors.</b>

26
00:02:15.375 --> 00:02:19.250
<b>This happens with pleasurable desires too.</b>

27
00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:22.208
<b>You're trying to concentrate,</b>

28
00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:23.750
<b>but the senses,</b>

29
00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:30.166
<b>can distract your mind by reminding </b>
<b>it of some past pleasure.</b>

30
00:02:30.166 --> 00:02:31.041
<b>Therefore,</b>

31
00:02:31.041 --> 00:02:36.875
<b>it's crucial to keep gathering </b>
<b>new and better experiences in life.</b>

32
00:02:36.875 --> 00:02:40.958
<b>Keep refreshing the old impressions </b>
<b>etched on your mind.</b>

33
00:02:40.958 --> 00:02:42.541
<b>Old desires,</b>

34
00:02:42.541 --> 00:02:43.791
<b>old fears...</b>

35
00:02:43.791 --> 00:02:47.666
<b>both hinder progress.</b>

36
00:02:52.625 --> 00:02:58.000
<b>My purpose here is to awaken Arjuna.</b>

37
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.875
<b>Our senses</b>

38
00:03:00.875 --> 00:03:06.250
<b>are not only restless, but incredibly powerful.</b>

39
00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:11.958
<b>anyone who believes that </b>
<b>through willpower alone,</b>

40
00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:16.750
<b>they can fully control their desires.</b>

41
00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:22.166
<b>It would be a grave mistake.</b>

42
00:03:22.166 --> 00:03:25.958
<b>You must have experienced this yourself.</b>

43
00:03:25.958 --> 00:03:32.958
<b>You may have decided to watch</b>
<b>just one episode of a series,</b>

44
00:03:32.958 --> 00:03:38.166
<b>but before you knew it, time slipped away.</b>

45
00:03:38.166 --> 00:03:43.125
<b>Important tasks were left undone.</b>

46
00:03:43.125 --> 00:03:48.833
<b>The doctor strictly advised diet control,</b>

47
00:03:48.833 --> 00:03:53.958
<b>but the moment something tasty </b>
<b>touched your tongue, temptation took over,</b>

48
00:03:53.958 --> 00:04:01.833
<b>you overate, control was lost once again.</b>

49
00:04:01.833 --> 00:04:04.416
<b>Think of it this way</b>

50
00:04:04.416 --> 00:04:13.333
<b>in terms of physical strength, between a horse </b>
<b>and a human, the horse will always be stronger.</b>

51
00:04:13.333 --> 00:04:19.041
<b>A rider cannot control it through force alone.</b>

52
00:04:19.041 --> 00:04:23.750
<b>A skilled horseman needs </b>
<b>continuous practice, experience,</b>

53
00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.583
<b>and</b>

54
00:04:25.583 --> 00:04:30.333
<b>humility to acknowledge the horse's strength.</b>

55
00:04:30.333 --> 00:04:31.416
<b>Similarly,</b>

56
00:04:31.416 --> 00:04:35.791
<b>humans need new experiences,</b>
<b>constant practice,</b>

57
00:04:35.791 --> 00:04:43.375
<b>and the humility to accept that the </b>
<b>power of our senses far exceeds our own.</b>

58
00:04:43.375 --> 00:04:51.958
<b>With this humble approach, one can gradually</b>
<b>transform the desires of their senses.</b>

59
00:04:56.625 --> 00:05:05.875
<b>When children from well-educated, refined </b>
<b>families stray toward uncouth behavior,</b>

60
00:05:05.875 --> 00:05:16.333
<b>it's not just painful for parents it seems </b>
<b>incomprehensible.They struggle to understand</b>

61
00:05:16.333 --> 00:05:25.041
<b>that despite the best schools, higher education, </b>
<b>and all possible resources how did this happen.</b>

62
00:05:25.041 --> 00:05:27.083
<b>Usually,</b>

63
00:05:27.083 --> 00:05:31.958
<b>this realization comes far too late.</b>

64
00:05:31.958 --> 00:05:34.041
<b>Perhaps because</b>

65
00:05:34.041 --> 00:05:37.625
<b>the seed of such behavior </b>

66
00:05:37.625 --> 00:05:41.625
<b>was planted somewhere in childhood itself.</b>

67
00:05:41.625 --> 00:05:43.250
<b>Premium schools,</b>

68
00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:44.416
<b>higher education,</b>

69
00:05:44.416 --> 00:05:45.625
<b>resources...</b>

70
00:05:45.625 --> 00:05:49.708
<b>these are all external factors.</b>

71
00:05:49.708 --> 00:05:55.791
<b>Beyond these, there are numerous </b>
<b>situations both inside and outside the home</b>

72
00:05:55.791 --> 00:06:01.500
<b>where a child gains various experiences.</b>

73
00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:05.750
<b>A child cannot distinguish between</b>
<b>right and wrong,</b>

74
00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:12.875
<b>and all these experiences impact </b>
<b>their impressionable senses.</b>

75
00:06:12.875 --> 00:06:15.458
<b>For instance</b>

76
00:06:15.458 --> 00:06:19.625
<b>consider the type of entertainment </b>
<b>preferred at home,</b>

77
00:06:19.625 --> 00:06:24.875
<b>the kinds of programs or films watched.</b>

78
00:06:24.875 --> 00:06:34.250
<b>Parents often overlook young age, </b>
<b>thinking a child won't understand.</b>

79
00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:38.666
<b>But it's not just about understanding.</b>

80
00:06:38.666 --> 00:06:41.416
<b>It's crucial to recognize</b>

81
00:06:41.416 --> 00:06:43.791
<b>that at any age,</b>

82
00:06:43.791 --> 00:06:48.125
<b>senses and their desire for experiences</b>

83
00:06:48.125 --> 00:06:52.125
<b>are fundamental to human nature.</b>

84
00:06:52.125 --> 00:06:55.208
<b>Every experience leaves its mark.</b>

85
00:06:55.208 --> 00:06:56.791
<b>Moreover,</b>

86
00:06:56.791 --> 00:06:59.583
<b>parents sometimes forget</b>

87
00:06:59.583 --> 00:07:06.583
<b>that many sources of temptation are </b>
<b>available at home even in their absence.</b>

88
00:07:06.583 --> 00:07:09.166
<b>It's important to understand</b>

89
00:07:09.166 --> 00:07:11.875
<b>that children are more impressionable,</b>

90
00:07:11.875 --> 00:07:17.833
<b>their senses just as active as an adult's,</b>

91
00:07:17.833 --> 00:07:22.708
<b>and impressions made on them don't easily fade.</b>

92
00:07:22.708 --> 00:07:27.916
<b>The senses are like that horse </b>
<b>on the right path,</b>

93
00:07:27.916 --> 00:07:29.833
<b>they'll lead to the destination,</b>

94
00:07:29.833 --> 00:07:31.583
<b>but</b>

95
00:07:31.583 --> 00:07:38.375
<b>if they stray, they'll plunge into a deep ravine.</b>

96
00:07:38.375 --> 00:07:47.666
<b>Parents must control media exposure</b>
<b>as much as possible.</b>

97
00:07:47.666 --> 00:07:55.666
<b>They should regularly discuss other </b>
<b>experiences with their children.</b>

98
00:07:55.666 --> 00:08:00.250
<b>Prevention is better than regret.</b>

99
00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:08.333
<b>Merely knowing right from wrong isn't enough.</b>

100
00:08:08.333 --> 00:08:15.416
<b>Sometimes, pride in one's self-control </b>
<b>becomes the very cause of regret.</b>

101
00:08:15.416 --> 00:08:17.083
<b>In professional life,</b>

102
00:08:17.083 --> 00:08:20.208
<b>you must have seen examples</b>

103
00:08:20.208 --> 00:08:26.000
<b>where a senior official said something insulting</b>

104
00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:30.958
<b>or behaved inappropriately with someone.</b>

105
00:08:30.958 --> 00:08:32.166
<b>And</b>

106
00:08:32.166 --> 00:08:40.291
<b>that one mistake destroyed a lifetime </b>
<b>of earned respect in an instant.</b>

107
00:08:40.291 --> 00:08:44.375
<b>Did they not know right or wrong?</b>

108
00:08:44.375 --> 00:08:45.750
<b>Of course they did.</b>

109
00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:49.125
<b>Did they lack self-control? </b>

110
00:08:49.125 --> 00:08:51.833
<b>Certainly not.</b>

111
00:08:51.833 --> 00:08:55.083
<b>Yet the mistake happened.</b>

112
00:08:55.083 --> 00:09:00.583
<b>They were careless in underestimating </b>
<b>the power of sensory desires.</b>

113
00:09:00.583 --> 00:09:08.666
<b>In an environment full of temptations, </b>
<b>attractions, and provocations</b>

114
00:09:08.666 --> 00:09:13.250
<b>such mistakes cannot be ruled out.</b>

115
00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:16.916
<b>Merely knowing right from wrong isn't sufficient.</b>

116
00:09:16.916 --> 00:09:20.083
<b>What's necessary is to remain not just confident,</b>

117
00:09:20.083 --> 00:09:20.916
<b>but</b>

118
00:09:20.916 --> 00:09:24.458
<b>vigilant about your senses at</b>
<b>every moment.</b>

119
00:09:24.458 --> 00:09:26.500
<b>Stay alert.</b>

120
00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:30.500
<b>External control over desires isn't enough;</b>

121
00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:34.541
<b>they must be completely overcome.</b>

122
00:09:34.541 --> 00:09:37.958
<b>This is a daily practice.</b>

123
00:09:37.958 --> 00:09:43.208
<b>The spiritual journey will assist you in this path.</b>

